I arrive at the small bakery on the corner.
I go into the warm shop.
It smells lovely of coffee and cake.
A baker in a white apron stands behind the counter.
"Good afternoon," the baker says.
"How can I help?" he asks.
I look at the many cakes.
I am buying a cake for tonight.
I point at a nice chocolate cake.
"I would like the chocolate cake, please," I say.
"Of course," the baker answers.
He puts the cake in a white box.
"That will be sixty-five kroner," he says.
I take my wallet out of my bag.
I pay the sixty-five kroner.
"Thank you very much, and have a good evening," the baker says.
"Thank you, you too," I answer.
I take the white box.
I walk carefully out of the shop with the cake.
